  "preamble": "A coda rhotic can assimilate completely to a following sibilant, giving a geminate [ss]. In Middle Indo-Aryan, Sanskrit r assimilated to a following stop, nasal, sibilant or v (Wikipedia gives varṣa → vassa), and Pali has only one sibilant, s, so Sanskrit rṣ and rś both appear as ss. Both etyma here have such a cluster: rṣ in varṣá and rś in dárśana.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Total Assimilation, Regressive Assimilation, Gemination",
